WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.664 --> 00:05.869 align:center line:79%
In May 2021, while visiting the renovation
work of the Salt Lake Temple,

00:06.303 --> 00:11.842 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson marveled
at the efforts of the pioneers who,

00:11.875 --> 00:17.714 align:center line:79%
with limited resources and unwavering
faith, built that sacred edifice,

00:17.748 --> 00:23.353 align:center line:79%
a physical and spiritual masterpiece
that has stood the test of time.

00:24.254 --> 00:28.292 align:center line:79%
However, he also
observed the effects of erosion,

00:28.825 --> 00:33.931 align:center line:79%
which over time had caused gaps
in the temple's original foundation stones

00:34.231 --> 00:36.433 align:center line:81%
and instability in the masonry,

00:37.267 --> 00:41.238 align:center line:79%
clear signs of the need
for structural reinforcement.

00:42.239 --> 00:46.543 align:center line:79%
Our beloved prophet then taught
us that just as it was necessary

00:46.543 --> 00:52.382 align:center line:79%
to implement major measures to strengthen
the foundation of the temple in order

00:52.382 --> 00:55.352 align:center line:81%
for it to withstand the forces of nature,

00:55.819 --> 00:59.389 align:center line:79%
we also need to take
extraordinary measures—

00:59.790 --> 01:06.296 align:center line:79%
perhaps measures we have never
before taken—to strengthen our

01:06.330 --> 01:08.865 align:center line:81%
own spiritual foundation in Jesus Christ.

01:10.133 --> 01:12.035 align:center line:81%
In his memorable message,

01:12.269 --> 01:16.807 align:center line:79%
He left us with two profound questions
for personal reflection:

01:18.208 --> 01:20.510 align:center line:81%
“How firm is your foundation?”

01:21.178 --> 01:23.981 align:center line:81%
and “What reinforcements to your testimony

01:23.981 --> 01:26.650 align:center line:79%
and understanding
of the gospel are needed?”

01:28.051 --> 01:33.123 align:center line:79%
The gospel of Jesus Christ
provides us with divinely inspired

01:33.123 --> 01:38.128 align:center line:79%
and effective means to prevent
the spiritual erosion in our souls,

01:38.528 --> 01:44.134 align:center line:79%
powerfully reinforcing our foundation
and helping us avoid gaps in our faith

01:44.401 --> 01:47.204 align:center line:81%
and instability in both our testimony

01:47.471 --> 01:50.974 align:center line:79%
and our understanding
of the sacred truths of the gospel.

01:52.142 --> 01:57.047 align:center line:79%
One particularly relevant principle
for achieving this purpose is found

01:57.047 --> 01:59.783 align:center line:79%
in section 12 of the Doctrine
and Covenants,

02:00.250 --> 02:04.521 align:center line:79%
a revelation given through
the Prophet Joseph Smith to Joseph Knight,

02:05.055 --> 02:10.761 align:center line:79%
a righteous man who earnestly
sought to understand the Lord’s will, not

02:10.761 --> 02:16.500 align:center line:79%
for mere outward change, but
to stand unwavering in his discipleship—

02:16.967 --> 02:19.202 align:center line:81%
firm as the pillars of heaven.

02:20.203 --> 02:24.941 align:center line:79%
The Lord declared:
“Behold, I speak unto you,

02:25.442 --> 02:31.148 align:center line:79%
and also to all those who have desires
to bring forth and establish this work;

02:31.948 --> 02:34.451 align:center line:79%
“And no one can assist
in this work,

02:34.451 --> 02:38.755 align:center line:79%
except he shall be humble
and full of love,

02:39.122 --> 02:44.428 align:center line:79%
having faith, hope, and charity,
being temperate in all things,

02:44.761 --> 02:48.265 align:center line:79%
whatsoever shall be
entrusted to his care.”

02:50.067 --> 02:51.868 align:center line:81%
The Savior’s guidance, recorded

02:51.868 --> 02:57.074 align:center line:79%
in this sacred revelation, reminds
us that temperance is an essential

02:57.074 --> 03:01.211 align:center line:79%
reinforcement for a firm
foundation in Jesus Christ.

03:01.812 --> 03:04.281 align:center line:81%
It is one of the indispensable virtues,

03:04.581 --> 03:07.350 align:center line:79%
not only for those who have
been called to serve,

03:07.684 --> 03:11.621 align:center line:79%
but for all who have made
sacred covenants with the Lord

03:11.955 --> 03:14.791 align:center line:81%
and accept to follow Him faithfully.

03:15.826 --> 03:17.494 align:center line:81%
Temperance harmonizes

03:17.494 --> 03:20.997 align:center line:79%
and strengthens other
Christlike attributes mentioned

03:20.997 --> 03:26.703 align:center line:79%
in this revelation: humility,
faith, hope, charity,

03:27.237 --> 03:29.773 align:center line:81%
and the pure love that flows from Him.

03:30.540 --> 03:34.211 align:center line:79%
Furthermore, cultivating
temperance is a meaningful way

03:34.211 --> 03:39.382 align:center line:79%
to protect our souls against
the subtle yet constant spiritual

03:39.416 --> 03:43.754 align:center line:79%
erosion caused by worldly
influences that can weaken

03:43.787 --> 03:45.956 align:center line:81%
our foundation in Jesus Christ.

03:47.257 --> 03:50.961 align:center line:79%
Among the qualities that adorn
true disciples of Christ,

03:51.461 --> 03:55.665 align:center line:79%
temperance stands out
as a reflection of the Savior Himself,

03:56.266 --> 04:00.103 align:center line:79%
a precious fruit
of the Spirit available to all

04:00.137 --> 04:03.106 align:center line:81%
who open themselves to divine influence.

04:04.107 --> 04:06.977 align:center line:79%
It is the virtue that brings
harmony to the heart,

04:07.344 --> 04:11.348 align:center line:79%
shaping desires and emotions
with wisdom and calmness.

04:12.149 --> 04:17.921 align:center line:79%
In the scriptures, temperance is presented
as an essential part of the progress

04:18.054 --> 04:23.326 align:center line:79%
in our spiritual journey,
leading us toward patience, godliness,

04:23.527 --> 04:29.366 align:center line:79%
and compassion while refining
our feelings, our words, and our actions.

04:30.400 --> 04:32.502 align:center line:81%
Disciples of Christ who strive

04:32.502 --> 04:37.374 align:center line:79%
to cultivate this Christlike
attribute become increasingly

04:37.374 --> 04:39.109 align:center line:81%
humble and full of love.

04:39.910 --> 04:42.612 align:center line:81%
A serene strength arises in them,

04:43.046 --> 04:48.285 align:center line:79%
and they become better capable
of restraining anger, nurturing patience,

04:48.585 --> 04:52.689 align:center line:79%
and treating others with tolerance,
respect, and dignity,

04:53.123 --> 04:56.626 align:center line:79%
even when the winds
of adversity blow fiercely.

04:57.727 --> 05:00.430 align:center line:81%
They strive not to act impulsively,

05:00.864 --> 05:05.802 align:center line:79%
but choose to act with spiritual
wisdom, guided by meekness

05:05.802 --> 05:08.605 align:center line:79%
and the gentle influence
of the holy Spirit.

05:09.372 --> 05:15.212 align:center line:79%
In this way, they become less vulnerable
to spiritual erosion because,

05:15.245 --> 05:17.180 align:center line:81%
as the Apostle Paul taught,

05:18.582 --> 05:24.120 align:center line:79%
they know that they can do all things
through Christ who strengthens them,

05:24.120 --> 05:28.758 align:center line:79%
even in the face of trials
that could shake their testimony of Him.

05:29.960 --> 05:31.728 align:center line:81%
In his epistle to Titus,

05:32.195 --> 05:36.633 align:center line:79%
Paul conveyed sacred counsel
regarding the qualifications of those

05:37.033 --> 05:42.372 align:center line:79%
who desire to represent the Savior
and do His will with faith and dedication.

05:43.206 --> 05:48.478 align:center line:79%
He said they should be hospitable,
sober, just, and holy—

05:49.012 --> 05:53.383 align:center line:79%
qualities that clearly
reflect the influence of temperance.

05:54.284 --> 06:01.424 align:center line:79%
However, Paul warned that they should
be “not self-willed, not soon angry, ...

06:02.125 --> 06:03.526 align:center line:81%
[and] no striker.”

06:04.761 --> 06:08.598 align:center line:79%
Such characteristics are contrary
to the mind of the Savior

06:08.832 --> 06:11.001 align:center line:81%
and hinder true spiritual growth.

06:11.735 --> 06:15.372 align:center line:79%
In the scriptural context,
“not self-willed”

06:15.672 --> 06:20.977 align:center line:79%
is one who refuses
to act with arrogance and pride;

06:21.711 --> 06:26.950 align:center line:79%
“not soon angry” is one who avoids
the natural urge to become impatient

06:26.950 --> 06:32.355 align:center line:79%
and irritated; and “no
striker” refers to one

06:32.389 --> 06:34.958 align:center line:81%
who rejects contention,

06:34.991 --> 06:39.562 align:center line:79%
aggressive, and harsh behavior verbally,
physically, and emotionally.

06:40.463 --> 06:44.134 align:center line:79%
As we strive to change our behavior
with faith and humility,

06:44.668 --> 06:51.241 align:center line:79%
we can be firmly anchored to the solid
rock of His grace and become pure

06:51.541 --> 06:54.911 align:center line:79%
and polished instruments
in His holy hands.

06:55.779 --> 06:59.716 align:center line:79%
In reflecting on the need
to cultivate the virtue of temperance,

07:00.183 --> 07:05.021 align:center line:79%
I am reminded of the words of Hannah,
the mother of the prophet Samuel—

07:08.892 --> 07:09.960 align:center line:81%
a woman

07:12.162 --> 07:16.766 align:center line:79%
of remarkable faith,
who, even after great trials,

07:17.267 --> 07:22.138 align:center line:79%
offered a song
of gratitude to the Lord. She said,

07:22.973 --> 07:26.409 align:center line:81%
“Talk no more so exceeding proudly;

07:26.810 --> 07:34.084 align:center line:79%
let not arrogancy come out of your mouth:
for the Lord is a God of knowledge,

07:34.351 --> 07:37.087 align:center line:81%
and by him actions are weighed.”

07:38.221 --> 07:40.223 align:center line:81%
Her song is more than a prayer;

07:40.890 --> 07:44.961 align:center line:79%
it is a self-addressed invitation
to act with humility,

07:45.295 --> 07:47.163 align:center line:81%
self-control, and moderation.

07:47.864 --> 07:52.268 align:center line:79%
Hannah reminds us that true
spiritual strength is not expressed

07:52.268 --> 07:57.107 align:center line:79%
in impulsive reactions or haughty
words, but in temperate,

07:57.140 --> 08:01.011 align:center line:79%
thoughtful attitudes aligned
with the Lord's wisdom.

08:01.011 --> 08:04.948 align:center line:79%
Oftentimes, the
world exalts behaviors

08:04.948 --> 08:07.851 align:center line:81%
born of aggressiveness, arrogance,

08:08.251 --> 08:10.587 align:center line:81%
impatience, and excessiveness,

08:11.321 --> 08:15.525 align:center line:79%
often justifying such attitudes
by the pressures of daily life

08:15.892 --> 08:19.629 align:center line:79%
and the inclination toward
validation and popularity.

08:20.663 --> 08:25.802 align:center line:79%
When we turn our gaze away from the virtue
of temperance and ignore the gentle

08:25.802 --> 08:28.238 align:center line:79%
and moderating influence
of the Holy Spirit

08:28.238 --> 08:31.107 align:center line:81%
in our way of acting and speaking,

08:31.608 --> 08:34.544 align:center line:81%
we easily fall into the enemy's trap,

08:35.045 --> 08:39.315 align:center line:81%
which inevitably leads us to utter words

08:39.315 --> 08:42.919 align:center line:81%
and adopt attitudes we will deeply regret,

08:43.286 --> 08:47.690 align:center line:79%
whether in our social, family, or even
ecclesiastical relationships.

08:48.591 --> 08:52.796 align:center line:79%
The gospel of Jesus Christ
invites us to exercise this virtue

08:53.329 --> 08:55.632 align:center line:81%
especially in times of challenge,

08:55.999 --> 09:00.670 align:center line:79%
for it is precisely on these occasions
that the true character

09:00.670 --> 09:06.242 align:center line:79%
of an individual is revealed.
As Martin Luther King Jr.

09:06.276 --> 09:12.549 align:center line:79%
once said, “The ultimate measure
of a man is not where he stands in moments

09:12.549 --> 09:14.184 align:center line:81%
of comfort and convenience,

09:14.551 --> 09:19.322 align:center line:79%
but where he stands
at times of challenge and controversy.”

09:20.457 --> 09:25.161 align:center line:79%
As covenant people, we are called
to live with our hearts firmly rooted

09:25.161 --> 09:28.731 align:center line:79%
in the sacred promises
we have made to the Lord,

09:29.099 --> 09:34.270 align:center line:79%
carefully following the pattern He
established through His perfect example.

09:34.637 --> 09:37.040 align:center line:81%
In return, He has promised,

09:37.740 --> 09:42.412 align:center line:79%
“Verily, verily, I say unto you,
that this is my doctrine,

09:42.712 --> 09:47.717 align:center line:79%
and whose buildeth upon
this buildeth upon my rock;

09:48.184 --> 09:52.188 align:center line:79%
and the gates of hell
shall not prevail against them.”

09:53.456 --> 09:58.895 align:center line:79%
The Savior's ministry on earth was marked
by the virtue of temperance

09:58.895 --> 10:01.131 align:center line:81%
in all aspects of His character.

10:02.432 --> 10:04.200 align:center line:81%
Through His perfect example,

10:04.501 --> 10:06.102 align:center line:81%
He taught us to “be patient

10:06.102 --> 10:10.173 align:center line:79%
in afflictions, reviled not
against those that revile.”

10:10.940 --> 10:16.212 align:center line:79%
As He taught that we should not
give in to anger because of disputes

10:16.212 --> 10:22.285 align:center line:79%
and contentions, He declared, “Ye must
repent, and become as a little child.”

10:23.186 --> 10:25.221 align:center line:81%
He also taught that all

10:25.255 --> 10:30.894 align:center line:79%
who desire to come unto Him
with full purpose of heart must reconcile

10:30.894 --> 10:33.630 align:center line:81%
with those with whom they are angry,

10:33.930 --> 10:37.100 align:center line:79%
or with those who have
something against them.

10:38.334 --> 10:41.471 align:center line:79%
With a temperate attitude
and compassionate heart,

10:41.905 --> 10:48.411 align:center line:79%
He assured us that when we are treated
with harshness, unkindness, disrespect,

10:48.411 --> 10:53.216 align:center line:79%
or disregard, His kindness
will not depart from us,

10:53.650 --> 10:58.521 align:center line:79%
and the covenant of His peace
shall not be removed from our lives.

11:00.423 --> 11:03.159 align:center line:81%
A few years ago, my wife

11:03.159 --> 11:07.063 align:center line:79%
and I had this sacred privilege
of meeting with some faithful members

11:07.063 --> 11:09.566 align:center line:81%
of the Church in Mexico City.

11:10.633 --> 11:14.704 align:center line:79%
Many of them, either
personally or through their loved ones,

11:15.071 --> 11:19.742 align:center line:79%
had endured indescribable trials,
including kidnappings,

11:19.742 --> 11:23.313 align:center line:79%
homicides, and other
heartbreaking tragedies.

11:24.681 --> 11:31.421 align:center line:79%
As we looked into the faces of those
Saints, we did not see anger, resentment,

11:31.421 --> 11:33.323 align:center line:81%
or a desire for revenge.

11:34.023 --> 11:37.794 align:center line:81%
Instead, we saw a quiet humility.

11:38.761 --> 11:42.432 align:center line:79%
Their countenances,
though marked by sorrow,

11:42.832 --> 11:47.003 align:center line:79%
radiated a sincere longing
for healing and comfort.

11:47.804 --> 11:51.040 align:center line:79%
Even though their hearts
were broken by suffering,

11:51.808 --> 11:55.511 align:center line:79%
these Saints pressed forward
with faith in Jesus Christ,

11:55.979 --> 11:59.949 align:center line:79%
choosing not to let their afflictions
become gaps in their faith

11:59.949 --> 12:03.853 align:center line:79%
or cause instability
in their testimony of the gospel.

12:04.754 --> 12:09.993 align:center line:79%
At the conclusion of that sacred
gathering, we greeted each one of them.

12:12.161 --> 12:19.435 align:center line:79%
Every handshake, every embrace, became
a quiet testimony that with the help

12:19.435 --> 12:24.941 align:center line:79%
of the Lord, we can choose to respond
with temperance to the frustrations

12:24.941 --> 12:26.376 align:center line:81%
and challenges of life.

12:27.176 --> 12:32.582 align:center line:79%
Their quiet and unassuming example served
as a tender invitation

12:32.582 --> 12:36.853 align:center line:79%
to walk the Savior's path
with temperance in all things.

12:37.387 --> 12:41.691 align:center line:79%
We felt as we were
in the presence of angels.

12:42.592 --> 12:45.862 align:center line:81%
Jesus Christ, the greatest of all,

12:46.362 --> 12:50.466 align:center line:79%
suffered for us until
He bled from every pore.

12:50.867 --> 12:54.904 align:center line:79%
Yet He never allowed anger
to inflame his heart,

12:55.738 --> 13:01.311 align:center line:79%
nor did aggressive, offensive,
or profane words escape His lips,

13:01.778 --> 13:07.417 align:center line:79%
even amid such affliction. With perfect
temperance and unmatched meekness,

13:07.850 --> 13:09.852 align:center line:81%
He did not think of himself,

13:09.852 --> 13:15.525 align:center line:79%
but of each of God’s children—past,
present, and future.

13:16.225 --> 13:22.332 align:center line:79%
The Apostle Peter testified of Christ’s
sublime attitude when he declared: “Who,

13:22.699 --> 13:25.868 align:center line:81%
when he was reviled, reviled not again;

13:26.336 --> 13:29.172 align:center line:81%
when he suffered, he threatened not;

13:29.505 --> 13:33.576 align:center line:79%
but committed himself to him
that judgeth righteously.”

13:34.344 --> 13:37.013 align:center line:81%
Even in the midst of the greatest agony,

13:37.480 --> 13:41.050 align:center line:79%
the Savior demonstrated
perfect and divine temperance.

13:41.484 --> 13:45.822 align:center line:79%
He declared, “Nevertheless,
glory be to the Father,

13:46.122 --> 13:50.727 align:center line:79%
and I partook and finished my preparations
unto the children of men.”

13:51.794 --> 13:54.163 align:center line:81%
My beloved brothers and sisters,

13:54.564 --> 13:59.502 align:center line:79%
I extend an earnest invitation
to all of us to adorn our minds

13:59.502 --> 14:05.074 align:center line:79%
and hearts with the Christlike virtue
of temperance as a sacred response

14:05.074 --> 14:09.645 align:center line:79%
to the prophetic call
of our dear President Russell M. Nelson,

14:11.714 --> 14:17.420 align:center line:79%
As we strive with faith and diligence
to weave temperance into our actions

14:17.420 --> 14:20.757 align:center line:79%
and words, I testify
that we will strengthen

14:20.757 --> 14:26.262 align:center line:79%
and anchor our lives more securely
upon the sure foundation of our Redeemer.

14:26.662 --> 14:30.867 align:center line:79%
I solemnly bear my testimony
that the constant pursuit

14:30.867 --> 14:36.372 align:center line:79%
of temperance purifies our soul and
sanctifies our heart before the Savior,

14:36.639 --> 14:41.277 align:center line:79%
gently drawing us nearer to Him
and preparing us, with hope

14:41.277 --> 14:47.116 align:center line:79%
and peace, for that glorious day when
we shall meet Him at His Second Coming.

14:47.683 --> 14:54.190 align:center line:79%
I share these sacred words in the name
of our Savior Jesus Christ, amen.

